{%- comment -%}
  mm-feature — a promoted block sitting beneath a mega panel's column row.

  Params:
    label       heading, styled as a column label
    blurb       one or two sentences
    image       CDN url, landscape; ask for &width= on the url itself.
                The width/height on the tag are a 3:2 CLS hint matching the
                image in use, not a crop - CSS sizes it width:100%, height:auto.
    link        destination for both the image and the link line
    link_label  defaults to "Learn more"

  Renders nothing without a label, so a panel that has not set one costs no
  markup.

  12/09/2026: the block was a stack (heading, blurb, image, link) inside the
  last column and is now a card spanning two column tracks, image beside the
  words. Stacked, a box this wide would have shown a 457px image and made the
  panel taller, which is the opposite of what the change was for.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if label != blank -%}
  <div class="mm__feature">
    {%- if image != blank -%}
      <a class="mm__feature-img" href="{{ link | default: '#' }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="{{ image }}" alt="" width="180" height="120" loading="lazy">
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="mm__feature-words">
      <p class="mm__label">{{ label }}</p>
      {%- if blurb != blank -%}
        <p class="mm__feature-blurb">{{ blurb }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if link != blank -%}
        <a class="mm__feature-link" href="{{ link }}">
          <span>{{ link_label | default: 'Learn more' }}</span>
          {% render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 14 %}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
